{"id": "z1109", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Since density equal s mass over volume, water is actually denser than all three of those. So the answer would be none of them sink more than water because they are less dense than it. Water sinks into all three.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
