{"id": "z1157", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The animal that has live births is the humm ingbird. Hummingbirds are birds, and like most birds, they lay eggs rather than giving birth to live young. The other options— poodle, crocod ile, and trout—are also egg layers or lay eggs as well. So none of them give live birth except for the hummingbird in this list, even though it still starts with an egg inside its body before hatching.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1165", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Members of rock bands often perform with a. Flutes are more common in classical or jazz music, not typically in rock. Sandals and earplugs aren't usually worn during performances unless for specific reasons like comfort or hearing protection. Glo ves might be used occasionally, but they're not standard equipment. So, none of these options are typical for rock band members to wear while performing.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1173", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 19, "onset_chunk": 18, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Photosynthesis convert s carbon di oxide, water, and sunlight into carbo hydrates by mix ing carbons into so luble plant matter. So the correct answer is C: mixes carbs into soluble plant matter. This process provides the energy plants need to grow and develop.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1181", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is C, sp in less marine organisms such as card ialginous and gel atinous organisms. Tu na primarily feed on a variety of marine life, including small fish, squ id, and other sea creatures that fit their size and dietary needs. While they do consume some smaller marine animals like jellyfish and other soft-bodied organisms, the primary focus is on prey items that are abundant in oceanic environments.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 28, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1189", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Endangered pandas are sometimes confined to enclo sures to be viewed by the public. This is a common conservation practice where pandas live in protected areas or zoos designed to help them survive and also educate people about their need s. The other options like being dropped into vol canoes, found eating corn in North America, or made into steaks are not real situations for pandas as they are strictly protected.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 25, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1197", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The teacher wants to show how to combine two substances together. To mix them completely, we need things that blend well or dissolve into each other. Let' s look at the options: A is water and soda. Water can mix with soda pretty easily because they are both liquid s and tend to blend. B is water and oil. Oil does not mix with water; it separates into layers, so they don' t mix well. C is sand and rock s. These are solid materials that do not combine easily; they just stay separate unless mixed physically. D is salt and bark. Sal t might dissolve in water, but bark is a solid organic material that doesn't mix with either water or salt in a meaningful way for this purpose. So between these choices, water and so da will mix the best. Soda is often made with water as its base, so adding more water just makes it more diluted but still combined. Therefore, the best option for mixing completely is A, water and soda.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 49, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1205", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Evaporation causes puddles to become dried-out mud. When water in a puddle turns into vapor and disappear s, what's left behind is usually dry, compact ed mud. The other options are not correct because evaporation doesn' t speed up crop growth or cause flowers to bloom more; it actually removes moisture from the environment. It also doesn't fill irrigation ponds—it depletes them by turning water into gas.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 24, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1213", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Plants will most rely on bees for poll ination. Be es are known as important pollinators because they collect n ectar from flowers and, in the process, transfer pollen between plants, helping them reproduce and spread seeds. P ythons, salmon, rob ins, and cr aters do not play a direct role in plant pollination like bees do.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 21, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1221", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If a pot on the stove is described as hot, it means that the body of the pot is of high temperature. So the correct answer is A. The other options don' t fit because a hot pot can't be cold or wet at the same time.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1229", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The feet of D endrocy gn a utumnalis are primarily designed for walking. These birds are known as cr ow woodpeckers or laughing thrushes, and they' re adapted to navigate through forest s and underbrush on the ground. While their feet help them move around effectively, they don't have specialized features for catching prey or swimming. So, the correct answer is C, walking.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 21, "carrier_ended": null}
