{"id": "z1245", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The lunar cycle also changes the sun.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1253", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A place that is snowy has a large amount of frozen water. Snow forms when water vapor in the air freezes into ice crystals, typically at temperatures below freezing. These crystal s accumulate on the ground or other surfaces to form snow. So, while wind storms and rain might occur in snowy regions, the defining feature of a snow y area is its abundance of frozen water.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 21, "carrier_ended": null}
