{"id": "z1269", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Transplanting seed ling oaks primarily has a positive impact on D, the environment. This is because transplant ing helps restore and maintain forest s, which improve air quality, support biodiversity, and combat climate change by absorbing carbon dioxide. While it may have some indirect benefits like enhancing neighborhood aesthetics or potentially increasing housing value in certain areas, its most direct and significant effect is environmental.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 28, "carrier_ended": null}
