{"id": "z1853", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Edward had thirteen dollars. He spent some money, and now he has three dollars. To find out how much Edward spent, we can subtract the amount he has left from the amount he started with. So, thirteen minus three equals ten. That means Edward spent ten dollars.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1861", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Faye was placing her pencils and crayons into 3 0 rows with 7 1 crayon s and 2 4 pencil s in each row. How many pencils does she have? She has 30 rows, and each row has 24 pencil s. So, to find the total number of pencils, you multiply 3 0 by 2 4. That equal s 7 20. So, Fa ye has 7 20 pencil s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 29, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1869", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So the machine made 13 shirt s yesterday and 3 shirts today, for a total of 16 shirts. Since it makes 8 shirts per minute, we divide 16 by 8. That gives us 2 minutes in total.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1877", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Debbie bought 8 8 water bottles and drank four per day. So to figure out how many days the water bottle s would last, we just need to divide the total number of water bottles by the daily consumption. That' s 8 8 divided by 4, which equal s 22 days. So the water bottles would last for 22 days.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1885", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So Frank read a book with 1 9 3 pages split into 15 chapters. That means each chapter had about 1 2.8 7 pages on average. He finished the whole thing in 66 0 days. To figure out how many chapters he read per day, we divide the total number of chapter s by the number of days. So that's 15 divided by 66 0. That comes to roughly 0. 02 27 chapters per day.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 29, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1893", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Bobby ate 3 3 pieces of candy, then he ate 4 more. So that's 3 3 plus 4 equal s 37 piece s of candy. He also ate 14 pieces of chocolate. So altogether, Bobby eat 37 pieces of candy and 14 pieces of chocolate. That' s a total of 5 1 pieces of candy and chocolate altogether.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
