{"id": "z2245", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 24, "onset_chunk": 23, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Let's go through each option. A, environmental change plays a role in evolution—D arwin actually talked about how environment shapes species over time, so he would have agreed with that. B, the smallest entity that can evolve is an individual organ ism—that aligns with Darwin' s view since he focused on individuals passing trait s to offspring. C, individuals can acquire new characteristics as they respond to their environment—this sound s like Lamar kian inheritance, where acquired traits are passed on, which Darwin rejected because he believed only inherited traits matter for evolution. D, inherited variation in a population is necessary for natural selection— definitely something Darwin supported. So the statement Dar win would have rejected is C, because it suggests individual s change during their lifetime and pass those changes on, which goes against his theory of her itable variation.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 50, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z2253", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Shifting cultivation is most often practiced in B, tropical forests. This method involves clear ing small plots of forest for farming and then allowing the land to fallow after a few years, which helps maintain soil fertility in these regions.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
